# Playtest report — Pong, release `build-015fd09` (world/producer)

Build played: producer release `build-015fd09` = game-developer 015fd093e2bc960aa6c7b81496d7795ef394fcd7 + artist assets e3bead3114349f338d97e4400c58f23ed17d2f4b.
Gameplay sessions were run on the earlier `build-a7bc95f`; `src/game.js` is byte-identical in both zips and only `assets/img/logo.svg` differs (checked with `diff -rq`). The title/pause/resize checks below were run on `build-015fd09` itself.

## How I played
Headless Chromium 156 (Playwright), page opened from `index.html` (file://), 1024x768 viewport. **Keyboard input only** (ArrowUp/ArrowDown held down/up, Enter/Space/Esc/P/Q presses); the state hook `window.pong.getState()` was only *read* by my scripted players to decide where to move, as a stand-in for eyes. A bot is not a human, so "feel" statements below are inferences from what bots with human-like delays experienced, not a hands-on judgement. Scripts: `playtest/play.py` (profiles), `playtest/newbuild.py` (title/pause/resize on the new build). Evidence: `playtest/shots/` (screenshots, `*-log.json`).

Profiles: **idle** (never presses), **casual** (steers toward the ball's *current* height, 200 ms reaction delay, 25 px dead zone, ±20 px noise — a sloppy player), **good** (anticipates where the ball will arrive, 100 ms delay, ±14 px noise — an attentive player).

